  "question": {
    "text": "$A$ and $B$ are events such that $P(A \\cup B)=3 / 4, P(A \\cap B)=1 / 4, P(\\bar{A})=2 / 3$ then $P(\\bar{A} \\cap B)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "hQSAr",
      "text": "\n5/12\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "NtDnT",
      "text": "\n3/8\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Z8xuZ",
      "text": "\n5/8\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LxSCT",
      "text": "\n1/4",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$P(A \\cup B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A \\cap B) \\Rightarrow \\frac{3}{4}=1-P(\\bar{A})+P(B)-\\frac{1}{4}$\n$\\Rightarrow 1=1-\\frac{2}{3}+P(B) \\Rightarrow P(B)=\\frac{2}{3} ; \\quad$ Now, $P(\\bar{A} \\cap B)=P(B)-P(A \\cap B)=\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{5}{12}$",
    "image": null
  },
